  <div><strong>Trigger</strong> Pipeline gap of 3+ weeks with no inbound from organic / referral; or testing a new audience</div>
  <div><strong>Owner</strong> Jon</div>
  <div><strong>Time</strong> 4 hours setup, 30 min/week monitoring</div>
  <div><strong>Output</strong> Booked discovery calls at &le;$300/lead, tracked end-to-end</div>
</div>

<h2>When NOT to run paid ads</h2>
<p>Paid ads are not a substitute for missing organic / network presence. Run them only when:</p>
<ul>
  <li>The site is converting at a known rate (so cost-per-lead can be calculated honestly).</li>
  <li>The discovery-call SOP is tight enough to handle volume swings.</li>
  <li>I have at least 4 hours/week to monitor and iterate.</li>
  <li>There is a specific gap I am trying to fill, not a vague "more leads".</li>
</ul>
<p>If any of these are missing, the budget is better spent on cold outreach (M1) or content marketing (M4).</p>

<h2>Campaign structure (Google Ads, search-only)</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>One campaign per audience.</strong> Service-business-owner-by-trade is the audience. Start with one trade (HVAC) before fanning out.</li>
  <li><strong>One ad group per high-intent keyword cluster.</strong> "Custom website for HVAC", "HVAC website design", "HVAC website builder", "HVAC marketing website". Tight match-types only (phrase / exact). NO broad match.</li>
  <li><strong>Negative keyword list, aggressive.</strong> "Free", "diy", "template", "wix free", "tutorial", "course", "wordpress plugin". Updated weekly.</li>
  <li><strong>Geo-targeting:</strong> U.S. + Canada only. Exclude all other geos. Bid adjustment +20% for major metros, -50% for rural.</li>
  <li><strong>Day-parting:</strong> Tuesday-Thursday 8am-5pm local. Other times paused.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Landing page requirements</h2>
<p>Ads must NOT point at <code>/</code>. They point at a dedicated landing page:</p>
<ul>
  <li>One headline matching the ad copy almost word-for-word.</li>
  <li>One CTA: book a discovery call OR request a free 5-point audit.</li>
  <li>Trust signals visible above the fold: 95-100 PageSpeed claim, "I am Jon", $0 down.</li>
  <li>NO main nav. Logo + phone in header, footer minimal.</li>
  <li>Typical landing-page template lives at <code>/sop/landing-page-playbook/</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Conversion tracking</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Set up the conversion event in Google Ads tied to a successful form submission on the thank-you page.</li>
  <li>Pass a UTM through to the form so the lead row in the inbox carries source / campaign / ad group.</li>
  <li>Review weekly: which ad group drove the booked call, not just the form fill.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Budget framework</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Starter cap:</strong> $1,500/month, max $50/day, max $5/click.</li>
  <li><strong>Target CPL (cost-per-lead):</strong> &le;$300 for an audit request; &le;$500 for a booked call.</li>
  <li><strong>Lead-to-close rate assumed:</strong> ~20% on warm calls. So target effective CAC: $1,500-$2,500 per signed client.</li>
  <li><strong>Scale up rule:</strong> after 4 weeks of CPL at or below target, raise budget by 25%. Repeat until CPL drifts.</li>
  <li><strong>Kill rule:</strong> after 4 weeks of CPL above 2&times; target, pause. Audit the funnel; do not just spend more.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Steps to launch a campaign</h2>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Pick the trade and the audience (one only).</li>
  <li>Build the landing page (per <code>/sop/landing-page-playbook/</code>).</li>
  <li>Set up Google Ads conversion event.</li>
  <li>Build the campaign with one ad group, two ad variants, and a tight keyword list (10-15 keywords max).</li>
  <li>Add the negative keyword list.</li>
  <li>Set geo, day-parting, bid cap, daily cap.</li>
  <li>Launch on a Tuesday morning. Watch the first 24h closely; pause if obvious problems.</li>
  <li>Review weekly. Move budget to whichever ad group is generating booked calls (not just clicks).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Common issues</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>High clicks, low conversions.</strong> Landing page is the bottleneck. Audit the page; A/B the headline.</li>
  <li><strong>Low clicks.</strong> Ad copy or keywords are wrong. Rewrite ad; tighten keyword match types.</li>
  <li><strong>Conversions are bad-fit leads.</strong> Tighten the qualification questions on the form.</li>
  <li><strong>CPL drifts up.</strong> Negative-keyword sweep + audience refresh; do not just raise the bid.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Exit criteria</h2>
<ul>
  <li>4 consecutive weeks at or below target CPL.</li>
  <li>Booked-call quality is at least as good as organic / network leads.</li>
  <li>I am not spending more time managing the campaign than I am gaining in pipeline.</li>
</ul>
